Browser checks — run against the stalled tab, in this order. Each maps to one failure class and one bounded recovery.

  1. Visible tab — preview_status
     pass: preview_status reports available, not loading, no dialog, and its url matches the verified URL above. A false visible flag alone is not a failure; after activation, a successful same-tab snapshot confirms capture readiness while visibility confirmation remains unavailable.
     fail → browser-visibility: unavailable or perpetually loading tab, pending dialog, or a url that is not the verified one.

  2. Snapshot — preview_snapshot
     pass: a snapshot returns (image and page state).
     fail → browser-snapshot: timeout or error while check 1 passes.

  3. Viewport — preview_resize to 1280×900, then confirm the page's live size
     pass: the resize returns and a page read (window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight) reports exactly the target size — the resize's own echo and the status read's viewportSetting can both be stale.
     fail → browser-viewport: timeout, or a page read that differs from the target.

  Budget: At most three attempts per browser operation — the first failure plus two recoveries — with the class's recovery action between attempts. Three failed attempts is the whole budget; exhausting it ends recovery for this pass. Record, don't retry.

  After any successful recovery, before the pass claims anything again:
  1. Re-run the capture preflight against the exact URL before capturing — recovery keeps the same checkout and URL; if the port changed, preflight the new URL instead.
  2. Confirm capture readiness (preview_status: available, not loading, no dialog, verified URL; successful same-tab snapshot when visible is unreliable) and that the page is actually at 1280×900: a resize's own success is not a confirmation (its response can echo a stale size, and preview_status carries the requested setting), so read the live size in the page — window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight — when the status read shows only the setting. Then resume the pass at the same URL.

  Recovery rules: docs/agents/visual-evidence.md §5

